+# Pre-Ship Review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Scope: frontend (`packages/nextjs`) and its configuration. Static code review;
+addresses cross-checked against `deployedContracts.ts`. Contract-verification
+status on Basescan could not be confirmed programmatically (no API key) — see
+SB-6. Report only; no code was changed.
+
+Severity legend: **ship-blocking** = do not ship until fixed. **should-fix** =
+fix before real users, not a hard blocker.
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### SB-1 — No Connect Wallet button; plain text instead
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`
+```tsx
+{!isConnected ? (
+  <p className="mt-4">Please connect your wallet to send a payout.</p>
+) : ( ... )}
+```
+A disconnected user sees a sentence, not a way to connect. The whole payout flow
+is unreachable.
+**Fix:** render the connect CTA in that slot:
+```tsx
+import { RainbowKitCustomConnectButton } from "~~/components/scaffold-eth";
+...
+{!isConnected ? <RainbowKitCustomConnectButton /> : ( ... )}
+```
+
+### SB-2 — Uses raw wagmi `useWriteContract`, not `useScaffoldWriteContract`
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:6,21`
+```tsx
+import { useAccount, useWriteContract } from "wagmi";
+const { writeContractAsync, isPending } = useWriteContract();
+```
+`isPending` from wagmi flips back to `false` the moment the wallet returns a tx
+hash — i.e. before the tx is mined. Every gating decision below (button
+disable, allowance refetch) is built on a signal that fires too early.
+**Fix:** use the scaffold hook, which waits for block confirmation and gives
+readable errors:
+```tsx
+const { writeContractAsync, isPending } = useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "Payouts" });
+// separate hook instance for the USDC approve
+```
+
+### SB-3 — No network check; main CTA renders on the wrong chain
+`app/payouts/page.tsx` (entire action block)
+There is no comparison of the connected chain to Base (8453). On the wrong
+network the user still sees **Approve / Send Payout**, clicks, and eats a silent
+wagmi chain-mismatch error. The header `WrongNetworkDropdown` is not sufficient
+per SE-2 QA — the action button itself must become a switch button.
+**Fix:** branch the primary CTA on `useChainId() === targetNetwork.id`; on
+mismatch render a `useSwitchChain`-driven "Switch to Base" button in the same
+slot as Approve/Pay.
+
+### SB-4 — Approve and Send Payout shown simultaneously (no four-state flow)
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+Both buttons are always rendered side by side. There is no allowance read, so
+the UI never knows whether an approval is needed. Users will pay before
+approving (revert), or double-approve.
+**Fix:** read allowance
+(`useScaffoldReadContract` USDC `allowance(owner, PAYOUTS.address)`) and show
+exactly one primary button at a time: Connect → Switch network → Approve (when
+allowance < amount) → Send Payout. Re-check allowance after the approve tx
+confirms.
+
+### SB-5 — Double-submit not prevented; `disabled` only reads `isPending`
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:102,109`
+```tsx
+disabled={isPending}
+```
+Combined with SB-2, `isPending` drops at signature time, so the button
+re-enables while the tx is still unconfirmed — user can fire a second
+approve/pay. There is no `approvalSubmitting` (click→hash gap) and no
+`approveCooldown` (confirm→cache-refresh gap).
+**Fix:** two explicit states, both on the `disabled` prop:
+```tsx
+disabled={isPending || submitting || cooldown}
+```
+`submitting` set at top of handler, cleared in `finally {}`; `cooldown` set
+after the await resolves, cleared after a short delay + allowance refetch.
+
+### SB-6 — Confirm both contracts are verified on Basescan
+`contracts/deployedContracts.ts:9` (Payouts `0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2`),
+`:50` (USDC `0x8335…2913` — this is canonical Base USDC, already verified).
+Could not confirm the **Payouts** contract's verification from here.
+**Fix:** open the Payouts address on basescan.org; if the Contract tab shows
+bytecode only, run `yarn verify --network base`. Unverified = trust red flag for
+a money-moving app. Verify before ship.
+
+### SB-7 — SE-2 default branding still in place
+- Tab title: `app/layout.tsx:11` `title: 'Scaffold-ETH 2 App'`, and
+  `utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:8` template `"%s | Scaffold-ETH 2"`. Every
+  tab reads "… | Scaffold-ETH 2".
+- Footer: `components/Footer.tsx:50-74` — "Fork me" → scaffold-eth/se-2, "Built
+  with ❤ at BuidlGuidl", Telegram "Support" link.
+- README: `README.md:1` — default "🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2" template, not this
+  project.
+- Home page: `app/page.tsx` still "Welcome to Scaffold-ETH 2" with
+  edit-`page.tsx` scaffold copy.
+
+**Fix:** set app name/description in `getMetadata` + `layout.tsx` and change the
+title template; strip BuidlGuidl/Fork-me/Support from the footer (replace with
+the project's own repo link or nothing); rewrite README for this dApp; replace
+the home page (or redirect `/` → `/payouts`).
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### SF-1 — USDC registered in `deployedContracts.ts`, not `externalContracts.ts`
+`contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50`; `contracts/externalContracts.ts` is empty.
+`deployedContracts.ts` is auto-generated and **regenerated on every
+`yarn deploy`** — the manual USDC entry will be silently wiped, and every USDC
+read/approve on the payouts page breaks with no error. It works today only
+because no redeploy has happened.
+**Fix:** move the USDC `{ address, abi }` entry to `externalContracts.ts` under
+`8453` and never hand-edit `deployedContracts.ts`.
+
+### SF-2 — Hardcoded dark background bypasses the theme system
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:65`
+```tsx
+<div className="min-h-screen bg-black text-white">
+```
+Forces black regardless of the DaisyUI theme / `prefers-color-scheme`; the
+header `SwitchTheme` toggle does nothing on this page. Light-mode users get a
+black page (and `border-gray-700` on line 121 is likewise hardcoded).
+**Fix:** `className="min-h-screen bg-base-200 text-base-content"`, and use
+`border-base-300` for the payout cards.
+
+### SF-3 — Recipient uses a raw `<input type="text">` instead of `<AddressInput/>`
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84`
+No ENS resolution, no validation, no blockie/paste handling. `recipient` is then
+cast `recipient as \`0x${string}\`` (line 55) and sent unvalidated — a typo
+sends USDC into a bad/black-hole address.
+**Fix:**
+```tsx
+import { AddressInput } from "@scaffold-ui/components";
+<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="0x… or ENS name" />
+```
+
+### SF-4 — DaisyUI `loading` class applied to the button itself
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:101,108`
+```tsx
+className={`btn btn-primary ${isPending ? "loading" : ""}`}
+```
+The `loading` class on a `btn` replaces the entire label with a full-size
+spinner — looks broken.
+**Fix:** drop `loading` from the class; put an inline spinner inside:
+```tsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={...}>
+  {busy && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm mr-2" />}
+  {busy ? "Approving…" : "Approve"}
+</button>
+```
+
+### SF-5 — Payouts contract address is displayed nowhere
+`app/payouts/page.tsx`
+Users can't see which contract they're approving/paying. For a money app that's
+a missing trust signal.
+**Fix:** show it with the `<Address/>` component (blockie, copy, explorer link):
+```tsx
+import { Address } from "@scaffold-ui/components";
+<Address address={PAYOUTS.address} />
+```
+
+### SF-6 — No USD values next to USDC amounts
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:75` (balance), `:126` (event list), `:85-91` (amount input)
+Amounts render as bare "… USDC". USDC ≈ $1 so the fix is trivial and the trust
+gain is real.
+**Fix:** show `(~$X.XX)` alongside each amount; for the input, an
+`IntegerInput`/USD-labelled field.
+
+### SF-7 — `pollingInterval` left at the SE-2 default of 30000
+`scaffold.config.ts:24`
+```ts
+pollingInterval: 30000,
+```
+30s update lag makes new payouts / balance changes feel broken on an L2.
+**Fix:** `pollingInterval: 3000`.
+
+### SF-8 — RPC config is all defaults; risk of public-RPC rate limiting in prod
+`scaffold.config.ts:29,32` and `services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx:20`
+- `alchemyApiKey` falls back to the shared SE-2 `DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY`.
+- `rpcOverrides` is empty (only the commented example).
+- `wagmiConfig` keeps a bare `http()` transport in the fallback list, which hits
+  Base's public RPC (`mainnet.base.org`, rate-limited).
+**Fix:** set `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` (or a Base `rpcOverrides` entry) and
+**confirm the env var is actually set on Vercel** (`vercel env ls`), not just
+referenced in code. Consider dropping the bare `http()` fallback so it doesn't
+silently hit public RPC.
+
+### SF-9 — Errors are swallowed to `console.error`; user sees nothing
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46,59-61`
+```tsx
+} catch (e) { console.error(e); }
+```
+Revert reasons (insufficient allowance/balance, wrong chain, user rejection) are
+invisible to the user.
+**Fix:** use scaffold notifications + parser:
+```tsx
+import { notification } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth";
+import { getParsedError } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth";
+} catch (e) { notification.error(getParsedError(e)); }
+```
+(`useScaffoldWriteContract` from SB-2 also surfaces these automatically.)
+
+### SF-10 — Event history scans from genesis (`fromBlock: 0n`) on Base
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:32`
+Scanning Base from block 0 for the `Paid` event is slow and will get
+rate-limited; the "Latest payouts" list may hang or come back empty.
+**Fix:** start from the deploy block —
+`fromBlock: 33712450n` (Payouts `deployedOnBlock` in `deployedContracts.ts`).
+
+### SF-11 — Pill-shaped inputs: `--radius-field: 9999rem`
+`styles/globals.css:36,63` (both theme blocks)
+The default SE-2 value makes the recipient input, amount input, and the memo
+`<textarea>` fully pill-shaped and can clip content.
+**Fix:** set `--radius-field: 0.5rem;` in both `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks
+(theme-level, not per-component).
+
+### SF-12 — Phantom wallet missing from the wallet list
+`services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:20-28`
+List has MetaMask, WalletConnect, Ledger, Base Account, Rainbow, Safe — no
+Phantom. Many users can't connect.
+**Fix:** import and add `phantomWallet` to the `wallets` array.
+
+### SF-13 — No mobile wallet deep-linking on the transaction buttons
+`app/payouts/page.tsx` (Approve / Send Payout handlers)
+RainbowKit v2 does not auto-deep-link on mobile. After tapping Approve/Pay via
+WalletConnect the user is left on the dApp with nothing prompting them to sign.
+**Fix:** wrap each write in a `writeAndOpen` helper that fires the tx first, then
+`setTimeout(openWallet, 2000)`; detect the wallet from WC session data (not just
+`connector.id`); skip when `window.ethereum` exists (in-app browser). Apply to
+**both** approve and pay.
+
+### SF-14 — Confirm favicon and OG thumbnail are not SE-2 defaults
+`public/favicon.png`, `public/thumbnail.jpg` (referenced via `getMetadata.ts:13,53`)
+Both files exist but appear to be the shipped SE-2 assets. The OG image URL is
+built from `VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL` (absolute in prod, OK) — but the
+image content and favicon should be this project's.
+**Fix:** replace both with project artwork; verify unfurl on the production URL.
+
+---
+
+## Minor / nits
+- `app/payouts/page.tsx:120` uses `key={i}` for the event list — prefer a stable
+  key (`${log.transactionHash}-${log.logIndex}`) to avoid render churn with
+  `watch: true`.
+- `amount` input is `type="number"` with no bounds/decimal guard; entering more
+  than 6 decimals makes `parseUnits(amount, 6)` throw inside the handler (caught
+  only by `console.error`). Guard/round before submit.
+- No empty-input guard: with empty `recipient`/`amount` the buttons still fire a
+  doomed tx (`parseUnits("0", …)` / invalid address). Disable the action until
+  inputs are valid.

